From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Chunfeng Yun <chunfeng.yun@mediatek.com>
Subject: [PATCH] usb: xhci-mtk: wait for u3 mac to be out of reset when
 enabling host

The u3 mac reset is not checked in xhci_mtk_host_enable(), so the
driver may go on before the u3 mac gets out of reset, then the u3
port is brought up unstable, and the attached SuperSpeed device can
be reset by the USB core again and again, e.g.

  usb 2-1.4: reset SuperSpeed USB device number 4 using xhci-mtk

Add STS1_U3_MAC_RST (BIT(16) of ip_pw_sts1) into the check_val when
there is at least one enabled u3 port, the same as mainline does
with "if (mtk->num_u3_ports > u3_ports_disabled)".

Adapted to linux-4.4.194 (ramips/mt7621): this kernel has no
mediatek,u3p-dis-msk / u3_ports_disabled support, so the condition
is simply "num_u3_ports > 0".

Signed-off-by: Chunfeng Yun <chunfeng.yun@mediatek.com>
[Backported to 4.4.194 by HiGarfield]
Signed-off-by: HiGarfield <HiGarfield@126.com>
---
--- a/drivers/usb/host/xhci-mtk.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/host/xhci-mtk.c
@@ -43,6 +43,7 @@
 
 /* ip_pw_sts1 register */
 #define STS1_IP_SLEEP_STS	BIT(30)
+#define STS1_U3_MAC_RST		BIT(16)
 #define STS1_XHCI_RST		BIT(11)
 #define STS1_SYS125_RST	BIT(10)
 #define STS1_REF_RST		BIT(8)
@@ -122,6 +123,14 @@
 	check_val = STS1_SYSPLL_STABLE | STS1_REF_RST |
 			STS1_SYS125_RST | STS1_XHCI_RST;
 
+	/*
+	 * The u3 mac must be out of reset before going on, otherwise the
+	 * u3 port may be brought up unstable and make the attached
+	 * SuperSpeed device be reset again and again.
+	 */
+	if (mtk->num_u3_ports > 0)
+		check_val |= STS1_U3_MAC_RST;
+
 	ret = readl_poll_timeout(&ippc->ip_pw_sts1, value,
 			  (check_val == (value & check_val)), 100, 20000);
 	if (ret) {
